WEBVTT

00:08.750 --> 00:09.980
Feuer!

00:16.850 --> 00:18.300
What now?!

00:24.340 --> 00:26.880
Adjusting one's firepower is not easy.

00:27.130 --> 00:28.970
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:28.970 --> 00:31.770
You don't need all this crazy
stuff just to make gyoza.

00:32.790 --> 00:34.790
Why?! Why?!

00:34.790 --> 00:36.890
How do I achieve it?!

00:36.890 --> 00:38.600
How do I achieve the

00:38.600 --> 00:41.880
Jet-Black Harmony that struck my heart so?!

02:15.110 --> 02:18.110
Great Bach-sama, should we not

02:18.110 --> 02:20.740
quickly recover those ClassicaLoids?

02:20.740 --> 02:22.660
We have intel that suggests

02:22.660 --> 02:24.880
their Musik has been witnessed.

02:24.880 --> 02:27.340
We must hurry, before
they cause a commotion.

02:28.660 --> 02:32.710
05: "Jet-Black Gyoza"

02:29.000 --> 02:30.410
Adagio.

02:30.410 --> 02:32.570
He says to just let them be.

02:32.570 --> 02:33.380
But...

02:33.880 --> 02:34.930
Allegro.

02:34.930 --> 02:36.200
Vivace.

02:36.500 --> 02:37.900
Presto.

02:37.900 --> 02:41.470
"More importantly, hurry
up and find that man."

02:41.470 --> 02:43.980
U-Understood.

02:51.690 --> 02:53.580
For crying out loud...

02:53.580 --> 02:54.710
What's up?

02:54.710 --> 02:55.920
Having a one-woman BBQ?

02:55.920 --> 02:57.230
What are you even talking about?

02:57.530 --> 02:59.440
Beethes-san made a mess.

02:59.440 --> 03:00.670
Making gyoza, again?

03:00.670 --> 03:03.450
Yeah. I don't know why he's
so obsessed with gyoza,

03:03.450 --> 03:07.300
but he loses sight of absolutely everything
else when he's focused on gyoza.

03:09.080 --> 03:11.170
He's kind of like your pops, huh?

03:11.170 --> 03:11.860
Huh?

03:12.180 --> 03:14.660
He was always locked away in his study.

03:19.790 --> 03:21.970
Dad, it's time to eat.

03:23.180 --> 03:24.010
Yeah.

03:27.180 --> 03:29.240
He's some kind of important
professor, right?

03:29.240 --> 03:33.110
Your dad was pretty weird, but he was cool.

03:33.110 --> 03:34.730
He wasn't cool at all.

03:35.250 --> 03:37.650
I don't care if it was for
his research or whatever.

03:37.650 --> 03:39.360
He kept racking up debt.

03:39.920 --> 03:42.600
Do you have any idea how much
my mom suffered because of it?

03:44.850 --> 03:47.830
Here, have some of this and cheer up.

03:48.130 --> 03:49.230
You like this, don't you?

03:51.230 --> 03:54.160
I ate so much as a kid,
I'm bored of it now.

03:54.480 --> 03:55.670
Come on.

03:55.670 --> 03:57.530
I went out of my way to buy it for you.

03:58.180 --> 04:00.200
You're so amazing, Tchaiko-chan.

04:00.200 --> 04:03.160
You understand everything Bach-sama says.

04:03.160 --> 04:04.960
I don't have a clue.

04:04.960 --> 04:06.760
It's not like I know, either.

04:07.230 --> 04:09.360
Not what that man is thinking deep inside.

04:10.560 --> 04:13.250
We do everything he insists.

04:13.790 --> 04:15.730
Is that truly the right thing to do?

04:16.020 --> 04:17.400
Tchaiko-chan...

04:17.760 --> 04:21.190
If we can bring those people back, we
may learn of the man's true intent.

04:23.000 --> 04:25.490
I'm counting on you, King.

04:30.900 --> 04:31.920
Hello?

04:33.860 --> 04:35.210
May I ask who's calling?

04:35.460 --> 04:39.160
I'm acquainted with Otowa Kyouko-san.

04:39.160 --> 04:40.310
My dad?

04:40.310 --> 04:41.180
Yes.

04:41.600 --> 04:45.060
There's something I'd like
him to return to me.

04:45.060 --> 04:46.470
Don't tell me... Money?

04:46.970 --> 04:50.100
Someone named King will
be visiting you shortly.

04:50.100 --> 04:52.820
Please return it immediately.

04:52.820 --> 04:55.410
But I don't have money to return!

04:56.100 --> 04:56.790
Who's that?

04:56.790 --> 05:00.780
How much trouble do you
need to make for me, Dad?

05:01.170 --> 05:03.070
Woohoo!

05:03.070 --> 05:04.190
Yay!

05:04.440 --> 05:06.510
What's up? Something fun?

05:06.510 --> 05:09.540
Lud-kun finished his new gyoza.

05:09.540 --> 05:11.200
You made more?

05:11.460 --> 05:14.800
My new piece is so incredible,

05:14.800 --> 05:17.960
I decided to share it with all of you.

05:18.460 --> 05:19.920
Want some, girl?

05:19.920 --> 05:21.460
I'll pass.

05:21.460 --> 05:24.580
Hey, it looks pretty good this time.

05:24.580 --> 05:25.920
Time to eat.

05:27.490 --> 05:28.380
Well?

05:28.380 --> 05:30.110
How is my masterpiece?

05:34.490 --> 05:35.260
Gross!

05:35.260 --> 05:36.710
What is this? What kind of idiot are you?

05:36.710 --> 05:38.040
Minus twenty points.

05:38.040 --> 05:40.150
It's unfathomably disgusting.

05:51.900 --> 05:52.830
See?

05:52.830 --> 05:55.750
What exactly is this pitch-black filling?

05:56.110 --> 05:57.930
The filling is perfectly normal.

05:57.930 --> 05:59.830
But the frying is revolutionary.

06:00.160 --> 06:02.920
I fry the filling really well first.

06:03.300 --> 06:07.170
Once it's charred black, I wrap it
in the skin that I'd fried prior.

06:07.710 --> 06:10.680
So you basically just
wrapped a chunk of ashes.

06:10.680 --> 06:13.350
Why does it not work?!

06:13.350 --> 06:15.800
Is this my fate?!

06:15.800 --> 06:18.910
No, I won't allow fate to defeat me.

06:18.910 --> 06:20.440
I will fight against fate

06:20.440 --> 06:24.440
and strangle it at its neck!

06:24.440 --> 06:25.890
Is he still not done with this?

06:25.890 --> 06:28.170
Just let him at it until he's done.

06:28.170 --> 06:32.030
The Jet-Black Harmony
Gyoza is special to him.

06:32.330 --> 06:34.240
Jet-Black Harmony?

06:34.240 --> 06:36.960
That sounds mysterious.

06:36.960 --> 06:38.940
Tell me more.

06:39.940 --> 06:40.830
Very well.

06:41.320 --> 06:42.830
A gyoza with

06:42.830 --> 06:45.580
a crispy skin and a soft, fluffy inside.

06:45.580 --> 06:48.340
That's the Jet-Black Harmony that I seek.

06:48.340 --> 06:50.490
A gyoza with a black filling?

06:50.490 --> 06:52.380
Today's gyoza was made with a

06:52.380 --> 06:54.860
secret technique for
making the inside black.

06:54.860 --> 06:58.770
I think it's a fine way to
bring out that blackness.

06:59.100 --> 07:02.270
So that's why you were trying
out so many ways to fry it.

07:02.530 --> 07:05.190
I've recreated the appearance perfectly.

07:05.190 --> 07:06.410
And yet...

07:07.750 --> 07:10.400
Just what am I missing?!

07:11.170 --> 07:11.780
Hey.

07:12.270 --> 07:13.170
What?

07:13.460 --> 07:17.090
Maybe the filling of that gyoza is made of

07:17.420 --> 07:20.450
stuff that's black to begin with.

07:26.410 --> 07:27.640
Here we are.

07:27.640 --> 07:29.200
Hurry up!

07:29.200 --> 07:30.450
Why do I have to come along?

07:30.450 --> 07:31.690
You're carrying stuff.

07:34.690 --> 07:37.130
I never thought they'd show up for me.

07:38.680 --> 07:41.350
Takamatsu Supermarket

07:38.820 --> 07:40.110
Let's see...

07:40.110 --> 07:42.850
Black foods.

07:41.350 --> 07:42.850
Black foods

07:43.770 --> 07:45.980
Sleep

07:44.580 --> 07:45.980
What? Why did that happen?

07:46.490 --> 07:47.680
What's up?

07:47.680 --> 07:50.970
I tried to look up "black foods,"
and it started acting up.

07:50.970 --> 07:52.760
It's cool.

07:52.760 --> 07:54.870
Let's just buy everything that's black.

07:58.870 --> 08:02.090
I never thought there'd be
so many kinds of black food.

08:05.370 --> 08:07.530
What are you looking at me so hungrily for?

08:07.530 --> 08:09.770
You're not getting any of this.

08:14.270 --> 08:17.050
You're not putting a paw on my stuff.

08:17.050 --> 08:20.180
Dude, I paid for all of this.

08:17.640 --> 08:23.640
Squid Ink Sauce

08:20.180 --> 08:21.020
Well, duh.

08:21.020 --> 08:22.380
It's for your sake, isn't it?

08:22.380 --> 08:23.640
For my sake?

08:23.870 --> 08:27.070
You pay money for me and Lud-kun.

08:27.070 --> 08:30.040
In turn, we make better progress
on our creative work.

08:30.340 --> 08:32.210
The works we create stimulate you,

08:32.210 --> 08:35.780
and your inspiration goes kaboom!

08:36.130 --> 08:37.070
Got it?

08:37.070 --> 08:38.840
I-I see?

08:40.010 --> 08:40.990
A mouse!

08:41.880 --> 08:43.970
A surprise attack! Coward!

08:44.350 --> 08:46.040
Hey, wait!

08:46.380 --> 08:48.880
Black Soy Beans

08:48.880 --> 08:51.380
Black Soy Beans

08:51.380 --> 08:53.880
Black Soy Beans

08:53.880 --> 08:54.970
Black Soy Beans

08:57.230 --> 08:58.530
I give up.

08:58.530 --> 08:59.580
I can't keep up.

09:01.430 --> 09:03.520
Those two sure are late.

09:03.950 --> 09:06.370
I wonder if they're having
trouble choosing foods.

09:06.670 --> 09:09.800
Maybe Beethes-san should have gone himself.

09:10.470 --> 09:11.480
I doubt he could.

09:11.920 --> 09:13.990
Look how depressed he is.

09:14.480 --> 09:16.610
It must have been a real shock

09:16.610 --> 09:19.060
to realize that the ingredients
themselves could have been black.

09:19.360 --> 09:21.940
It seems like something
you could figure out.

09:22.310 --> 09:22.990
Huh?

09:23.710 --> 09:24.770
Where's Cho-chan?

09:34.380 --> 09:36.440
Wait up!

09:36.440 --> 09:39.430
Cute little mousey-mouse!

09:39.960 --> 09:41.100
I'm home.

09:41.340 --> 09:42.510
You're late!

09:43.670 --> 09:46.280
You're late, you're late, you're so late!

09:46.280 --> 09:48.610
Stuff happened along the way.

09:48.910 --> 09:50.160
I thought you were depressed.

09:50.160 --> 09:52.100
Pleasure cannot be had without pain.

09:52.100 --> 09:53.860
Pain makes me stronger,

09:53.860 --> 09:56.840
so that I may have greater pleasures!

09:56.840 --> 09:58.280
You sure do recover quickly.

10:04.410 --> 10:05.700
Did you know?

10:05.700 --> 10:09.680
They call mice like you "mice in a bag."

10:09.680 --> 10:12.330
The mouse in the bag is you.

10:15.120 --> 10:17.590
So these are what you call "black foods."

10:17.590 --> 10:19.580
I see it. I can see it!

10:19.910 --> 10:21.650
Beyond this deep blackness is

10:21.650 --> 10:24.230
a glimmer of true hope.

10:24.530 --> 10:25.710
I'll fry it.

10:25.710 --> 10:29.400
I'll fry it all!

10:30.180 --> 10:32.350
Can't you at least thank me
for buying all this for you?

10:32.350 --> 10:33.350
It's all right.

10:33.350 --> 10:35.350
Look how happy he is.

10:35.350 --> 10:37.760
You've made yourself useful, tool.

10:38.060 --> 10:39.740
Do you really need to call me a tool?

10:40.220 --> 10:43.090
Oh yeah, where's Motes-san?

10:44.080 --> 10:45.920
He's playing tag with a mouse.

10:45.920 --> 10:46.690
What?

10:47.770 --> 10:49.040
Good work.

10:49.570 --> 10:50.870
Is that your mouse?

10:50.870 --> 10:52.260
Indeed.

10:52.260 --> 10:55.910
I bought that thing he's holding.

10:55.910 --> 10:57.130
Can I have it back?

10:58.630 --> 11:00.760
You're the one

11:01.680 --> 11:03.780
I'm having back.

11:03.780 --> 11:04.530
What?

11:04.530 --> 11:06.100
Come with me.

11:06.100 --> 11:09.100
Hey, what's the big idea?

11:09.510 --> 11:12.470
My name is King.

11:19.610 --> 11:22.700
Now, everyone, bring it on!

11:22.700 --> 11:25.030
I'll give it all my passion.

11:25.030 --> 11:27.700
Burn, burn, burn!

11:28.440 --> 11:31.170
Why do <i>I</i> have to help?

11:31.170 --> 11:32.300
Come on.

11:32.300 --> 11:33.790
It's a festival.

11:34.090 --> 11:35.090
It's done.

11:35.090 --> 11:37.210
Hurry up and bring it to him, tool.

11:37.210 --> 11:39.010
Please, stop calling me a tool.

11:39.010 --> 11:40.470
Feuer!

11:46.150 --> 11:47.560
What do you want from me?

11:47.560 --> 11:50.180
You're coming home where you belong.

11:50.180 --> 11:52.420
I have no idea what you're talking about.

11:52.420 --> 11:54.150
My home is at

11:54.450 --> 11:55.560
Otowakan.

11:57.380 --> 11:58.110
So fast.

11:58.610 --> 12:00.610
You aren't getting away from me.

12:00.910 --> 12:02.030
Move!

12:02.030 --> 12:04.700
Now, stop resisting and come!

12:15.170 --> 12:17.090
I knew it! You're afraid of cats!

12:19.270 --> 12:20.810
You bastard, give it a rest!

12:29.180 --> 12:30.060
No.

12:30.430 --> 12:32.510
They're all wrong.

12:32.510 --> 12:35.060
None of them have the flavor of

12:35.060 --> 12:36.840
the Jet-Black Harmony!

12:37.360 --> 12:38.820
Maybe you've done enough.

12:39.230 --> 12:40.400
I'm not giving up!

12:41.370 --> 12:43.170
That flavor exists.

12:43.170 --> 12:45.230
It <i>must</i> exist.

12:45.590 --> 12:47.620
Why are you so persistent?

12:48.010 --> 12:49.210
That flavor

12:49.860 --> 12:53.080
turns pain into pleasure.

13:03.650 --> 13:04.340
Come on.

13:05.340 --> 13:07.850
Stop making that face.

13:08.320 --> 13:09.850
Here, try this.

13:14.710 --> 13:15.760
It's good!

13:16.480 --> 13:18.370
Wh-What is this?

13:20.480 --> 13:21.730
My dad did that?

13:22.120 --> 13:23.490
For you?

13:24.020 --> 13:26.970
So you're trying to
recreate that nostalgic taste.

13:26.970 --> 13:29.070
You could have told us sooner.

13:29.400 --> 13:31.510
No one asked me.

13:32.830 --> 13:35.890
Anyway, I must search for that taste

13:35.890 --> 13:37.710
and achieve new pleasures.

13:37.980 --> 13:39.150
U-Um....

13:39.460 --> 13:41.480
Have this.

13:41.480 --> 13:42.590
Cho-chan.

13:42.930 --> 13:44.840
Why is Chopin-san, of all
people, making gyoza?

13:52.260 --> 13:53.070
You!

13:53.070 --> 13:54.440
How did you achieve this flavor?

13:54.440 --> 13:55.930
Hey, what are you doing?

13:58.190 --> 13:59.180
Is this...

13:59.650 --> 14:00.650
Bean paste?

14:00.950 --> 14:02.000
Bean paste?

14:02.000 --> 14:04.230
Mumble, mumble, mumble...

14:04.230 --> 14:07.070
Apparently, Cho-chan was searching online

14:07.070 --> 14:08.740
for gyoza with black filling.

14:09.380 --> 14:12.590
He ended up on a page with unusual sweets,

14:12.240 --> 14:15.290
Bean Paste Gyoza

14:12.590 --> 14:15.610
including crispy-skinned
gyoza with bean paste inside.

14:16.730 --> 14:17.930
It's sweet.

14:18.830 --> 14:20.090
It's that thing!

14:20.090 --> 14:20.750
What thing?

14:20.750 --> 14:23.450
It's that thing! You know, <i>that</i> thing!

14:23.450 --> 14:24.160
That thing?

14:24.160 --> 14:26.220
Yeah, it's that thing your dad

14:26.620 --> 14:29.970
made for us and the kids
from the neighborhood.

14:29.970 --> 14:31.140
Yum!

14:31.140 --> 14:32.480
Why is there bean paste?

14:32.480 --> 14:33.470
It tastes weird.

14:37.760 --> 14:40.600
This tastes a lot like that gyoza
from back then, doesn't it?

14:40.830 --> 14:42.430
Good job.

14:42.430 --> 14:45.530
Beethes is going to be freed from
his suffering, thanks to you.

14:45.530 --> 14:46.480
Not yet!

14:47.120 --> 14:50.380
This is indeed close to the
taste of the Jet-Black Harmony.

14:50.680 --> 14:53.930
But <i>something</i> critical is missing.

14:54.870 --> 14:55.850
It was

14:56.560 --> 14:58.000
sweet and spicy.

14:58.840 --> 15:01.100
Sweet and spicy?

15:09.150 --> 15:10.910
Sousuke, where's that stuff?

15:10.910 --> 15:11.570
Stuff?

15:11.570 --> 15:12.430
That stuff!

15:12.430 --> 15:13.890
The stuff from Hamanoya from this morning.

15:15.270 --> 15:16.990
Where did I put it?

15:16.990 --> 15:18.820
Hurry up and go find it!

15:18.820 --> 15:20.270
Okay.

15:20.890 --> 15:22.270
What is it, girl?

15:22.570 --> 15:24.210
Did you think of something?

15:24.520 --> 15:26.030
That was so fun.

15:26.420 --> 15:27.600
My, welcome home.

15:27.600 --> 15:29.140
You're back late.

15:29.140 --> 15:31.130
Man, get this.

15:30.330 --> 15:31.660
Shut up!

15:33.390 --> 15:35.330
You don't need to mention that.

15:35.330 --> 15:37.290
You'll ruin my dignity.

15:37.680 --> 15:39.070
Who are you?

15:39.380 --> 15:41.920
My name is King.

15:42.140 --> 15:43.210
King?

15:43.780 --> 15:45.790
Wait, from the phone call this morning?

15:46.030 --> 15:47.420
The very one.

15:47.420 --> 15:50.890
I should have come here to begin with.

15:50.890 --> 15:54.030
I'm sorry, I can't repay

15:54.030 --> 15:55.800
the money my father borrowed.

15:55.800 --> 15:57.680
I really don't have money.

15:57.680 --> 15:58.940
Money?

15:58.940 --> 16:02.200
I want the ClassicaLoids back.

16:02.590 --> 16:04.060
ClassicaLoids?

16:04.910 --> 16:06.470
Could you be...

16:06.470 --> 16:07.630
I am.

16:07.630 --> 16:11.450
You all were wasting time playing
about, so I came to take you home.

16:11.770 --> 16:14.410
But it's nice and comfy here.

16:15.670 --> 16:17.610
You disappoint me.

16:17.940 --> 16:20.710
Tchaiko-sama, I call on
you for your assistance.

16:26.130 --> 16:29.120
Pust' muzyka prinesyot

16:29.420 --> 16:32.770
vsem schast'e.

16:34.740 --> 16:36.000
Here we go

16:36.000 --> 16:42.730
Our dreams are already here

16:41.690 --> 16:43.510
Where did they come from?

16:42.730 --> 16:47.730
I won't let go

16:43.510 --> 16:45.980
They're here to take those two back.

16:46.760 --> 16:48.570
Get them!

16:48.060 --> 16:49.380
of this chance

16:49.380 --> 16:56.010
I'm going to shine

16:52.250 --> 16:53.930
Wait? Us, too?

16:53.930 --> 16:55.070
Don't touch me!

16:55.070 --> 16:56.820
I don't want to go home!

16:56.010 --> 17:01.250
I won't give up

16:58.180 --> 16:59.540
It's not working.

16:59.800 --> 17:01.250
Be silent!

17:01.580 --> 17:04.210
I've almost found the secret of

17:02.620 --> 17:05.790
Worrying won't solve anything

17:04.210 --> 17:05.790
the Jet-Black Harmony!

17:05.790 --> 17:09.370
Worrying won't solve anything

17:06.240 --> 17:08.210
Wh-What the hell?!

17:08.210 --> 17:09.370
They're kidnappers!

17:09.370 --> 17:11.040
Hurry up and help them!

17:09.370 --> 17:12.800
Rewire your brain

17:11.040 --> 17:12.050
You're joking.

17:12.800 --> 17:13.670
And everything—

17:15.160 --> 17:17.220
The secret to Dad's gyoza!

17:17.220 --> 17:18.350
What?!

17:31.190 --> 17:34.420
This is the secret to that gyoza?

17:39.450 --> 17:40.330
Beethes-san!

17:41.420 --> 17:42.690
This is indeed

17:43.580 --> 17:46.590
what I have been looking for!

17:49.600 --> 17:52.170
It flows through me.

17:52.580 --> 17:55.670
The melody within my heart flows through me!

17:55.920 --> 17:59.160
Spielen wir unsere

17:59.160 --> 18:01.220
Musik!

18:22.250 --> 18:23.340
It's futile!

18:23.340 --> 18:24.790
King is absolute!

18:23.840 --> 18:27.570
You who resist me

18:24.790 --> 18:26.870
No one can resist the power!

18:27.570 --> 18:31.310
Step aside and have shame!

18:28.020 --> 18:30.190
The king is absolute, you say?

18:31.310 --> 18:37.220
You're a thousand years
too young to fight me

18:31.630 --> 18:33.610
Lud-kun's Musik!

18:33.610 --> 18:37.010
Piano Concerto 5 in E minor.

18:37.220 --> 18:38.380
Also known as

18:39.270 --> 18:40.640
the Emperor Concerto.

18:39.510 --> 18:45.970
Foolish sewer rat,

18:40.640 --> 18:42.120
Very well.

18:42.120 --> 18:45.780
If you are the king, then I am

18:45.970 --> 18:47.350
the emperor who rules over you!

18:45.970 --> 18:55.780
Hark! All the power of the world
exists to cower before me

18:55.780 --> 19:10.020
The Emperor teaches the tyrannical
kings a lesson in nobility

19:10.020 --> 19:17.250
To admit defeat

19:10.590 --> 19:11.840
Wh-What...

19:11.840 --> 19:15.800
This is the power of the emperor?!

19:17.250 --> 19:23.460
Is itself courageous

19:23.830 --> 19:26.420
Forgive me, my emperor!

19:26.420 --> 19:32.760
Is itself beautiful

19:28.330 --> 19:32.330
All power cowers before mine.

19:32.330 --> 19:35.650
That is fate!

19:55.210 --> 19:58.030
Das Ende!

20:08.730 --> 20:10.660
He defeated my Musik.

20:10.660 --> 20:13.160
No way, your powers?

20:13.820 --> 20:14.860
Retreat.

20:16.160 --> 20:19.790
We can't underestimate their abilities.

20:23.100 --> 20:26.820
That man has saved me again.

20:34.120 --> 20:36.540
The Jet-Black Harmony.

20:36.540 --> 20:39.300
Enjoy it to your heart's content.

20:45.520 --> 20:48.080
Sweet and spicy?

20:48.730 --> 20:51.060
Hamanoya's miso manjuu, huh?

20:51.460 --> 20:54.930
To think Kanae's favorite snack would
be the secret ingredient for the gyoza.

20:54.930 --> 20:56.950
It's not really a secret ingredient when

20:56.950 --> 20:59.320
the filling is almost the
same as a miso manjuu.

20:59.620 --> 21:03.350
I wonder why Kanae's dad thought
to put this in his gyoza.

21:03.660 --> 21:04.570
This is

21:05.140 --> 21:07.200
the way that man lives.

21:08.930 --> 21:10.740
Did you enjoy it?

21:14.830 --> 21:16.880
That's the face I like to see.

21:16.880 --> 21:19.900
Nothing makes me happier than to

21:19.900 --> 21:23.040
see people enjoying something I made.

21:25.990 --> 21:28.100
The Jet-Black Harmony gave me

21:28.400 --> 21:31.720
light when I could hardly
even tell left from right.

21:32.020 --> 21:34.500
It is truly the dish of fate.

21:35.430 --> 21:37.460
This must be love.

21:49.680 --> 21:51.410
Did you enjoy it?

21:58.240 --> 22:00.920
Kanae's dad is so predictable, though.

22:01.240 --> 22:04.850
I wonder if this gyoza was the only
thing he could think as a treat for people.

22:04.850 --> 22:05.650
Wolf,

22:05.970 --> 22:08.090
Sleep

22:06.250 --> 22:09.550
why must you always ruin a good story?

22:09.780 --> 22:12.310
But I mean, it's weird enough that

22:12.310 --> 22:14.320
he'd try feeding ClassicaLoids gyoza.

22:14.320 --> 22:15.720
Hey, wait a second.

22:16.440 --> 22:19.160
What exactly is a Classica-whatever?

22:19.510 --> 22:22.070
Those people from earlier were
talking about that, too.

22:22.370 --> 22:24.120
Oh, haven't we told you?

22:24.420 --> 22:26.660
ClassicaLoids

22:27.010 --> 22:28.590
are us.

22:29.010 --> 22:31.660
ClassicaLoid?

22:31.930 --> 22:32.850
Yup.

22:32.850 --> 22:34.870
And they were created

22:35.900 --> 22:37.250
by me.

22:37.550 --> 22:38.840
Dad?

22:40.000 --> 22:43.000
To be continued

24:12.970 --> 24:27.780
06: "The First ClassicaLoids"

24:13.570 --> 24:16.860
The Great Bach says,
"Plan poco a poco;

24:16.860 --> 24:19.410
execute sforzando, adagio."

24:19.410 --> 24:22.140
But I desire a grand,

24:22.140 --> 24:24.070
boisterous gran-gran-grandioso.

24:24.070 --> 24:26.660
Oh, ClassicaLoids in danger!

24:26.660 --> 24:27.780
Something like that.

24:27.780 --> 24:28.870
See you then.
